---
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   /sample-brief — the brief we ran on ourselves.

   THE PUBLIC SAMPLE. /brief needs a "see a real one" and we cannot use a
   client's: the document names a real company and quotes their own pages back
   at them. So the sample is SeeSaw Labs' own brief, generated by the same
   pipeline with no special treatment — including the part where it tells us
   what we are missing. That is a stronger artifact than any example we could
   invent, and it is the only one that costs nobody their privacy.

   SERVED AS THE WHOLE RESPONSE, like /r/<token>. The brief is a complete
   document with its own head and styles; wrapping it in the marketing site's
   chrome would make it read as a page about a company rather than as the thing
   a lead receives.

   Regenerate with `npm run publish:sample -- <run dir>`, which is also where
   the banner and the indexable robots tag are added. Nothing is edited by hand
   — a sample that had been tidied up would be advertising a document we do not
   actually send.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import sample from '../content/sample-brief.html?raw';

/* Vite inlines the file at build time, so this route needs no filesystem
   access at runtime and cannot 404 on a missing bundle asset. */
export const prerender = false;

return new Response(sample, {
  status: 200,
  headers: {
    'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8',
    /* Public, unlike a real brief: it is marketing, and the publisher already
       flipped the document's own robots tag to match. */
    'cache-control': 'public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600',
  },
});
